    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.deps\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThe readme of plugin [abeldekat/harpoonline](https://github.com/abeldekat/harpoonline?tab=readme-ov-file#using-minideps-and-ministatusline) contains instructions for `mini.deps` and `mini.statusline`.\r\n\r\nThe plugin supports semantic versioning, so I experimented with the `checkout` option of `mini.deps`.\r\n\r\nI expected the output of `DepsUpdate` to contain lines of commits added after the latest stable version. I am not sure though if this expectation is justified.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.5\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nsetup:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nmkdir ~/.config/repro\r\ncd ~/.config/repro\r\n\r\nNVIM_APPNAME=repro nvim init.lua\r\n\r\n# Remove:\r\nrm -rf ~/.local/share/repro ~/.local/state/repro ~/.local/cache/repro\r\nrm -rf ~/.config/repro\r\n```\r\n\r\ninit.lua:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n\r\nlocal function clone(path_to_site)\r\n  local mini_path = path_to_site .. \"pack/deps/start/mini.nvim\"\r\n  if not vim.loop.fs_stat(mini_path) then\r\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\r\n    local clone_cmd =\r\n      { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--filter=blob:none\", \"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim\", mini_path }\r\n    vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\r\n    vim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim | helptags ALL\")\r\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installed `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal path_to_site = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/\"\r\nclone(path_to_site)\r\nlocal MiniDeps = require(\"mini.deps\")\r\nMiniDeps.setup({ path = { package = path_to_site } })\r\nlocal add, now = MiniDeps.add, MiniDeps.now\r\n\r\nvim.g.mapleader = \" \"\r\nnow(function()\r\n  vim.cmd.colorscheme(\"minischeme\")\r\n\r\n  add({ source = \"ThePrimeagen/harpoon\", checkout = \"harpoon2\", depends = { \"nvim-lua/plenary.nvim\" } })\r\n  local Harpoon = require(\"harpoon\")\r\n  Harpoon:setup({ settings = { save_on_toggle = true } })\r\n\r\n  vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>a\", function()\r\n    Harpoon:list():append()\r\n  end, { desc = \"Harpoon append\", silent = true })\r\n  vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>u\", function()\r\n    Harpoon.ui:toggle_quick_menu(Harpoon:list())\r\n  end, { desc = \"Harpoon ui\", silent = true })\r\n\r\n  add({ source = \"abeldekat/harpoonline\", checkout = \"stable\" })\r\n  local Harpoonline = require(\"harpoonline\")\r\n  Harpoonline.setup({\r\n    on_update = function()\r\n      vim.wo.statusline = \"%!v:lua.MiniStatusline.active()\"\r\n    end,\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  local MiniStatusline = require(\"mini.statusline\")\r\n  MiniStatusline.setup({\r\n    set_vim_settings = false,\r\n    content = {\r\n      active = function()\r\n        return MiniStatusline.combine_groups({\r\n          { hl = \"MiniStatuslineDevinfo\", strings = { Harpoonline.format() } },\r\n        })\r\n      end,\r\n    },\r\n  })\r\nend)\r\n\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n`MiniDepsUpdate`: The commits after the stable release are included in the report, below the line \"Monitor updates from main\".\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n\r\n![1711105025](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/58370433/6102d8c1-65a3-484b-aa04-0205c7a08465)\r\n\r\n![1711105114](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/58370433/cb79fc62-2748-4950-8887-f0a13c112a8a)\r\n\r\n\r\n`MiniDepsUpdate`: The commits after stable release `v1.2.1` are absent.",
