            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The `monitor` field is used to show *new* updates which were retrieved during the current update (`git fetch`, to be precise). This is done on purpose so as to not accumulate changes during long \"freezes\". Otherwise it might show wall of text if `checkout` target is frozen for a long time.\r\n\r\nSo in this case, if there is a new commit in `ThePrimagen/harpoon`, it will be shown in confirmation of the first `:DepsUpdate` run after it was pushed. During second and other runs it will not be considered as *new* change.",
