        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@echasnovski,\r\n\r\n> if there is a new commit in ThePrimagen/harpoon\r\n\r\nMinor clarification: The situation I described is about `abeldekat/harpoonline`\r\n\r\nI understand that any remote updates that already have been fetched will not be displayed.\r\n\r\n\r\nHowever:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n  add({ source = \"abeldekat/harpoonline\", checkout = \"v1.2.1\" })\r\n  require(\"ak.config.ui.mini_statusline\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n`DepsUpdate:`\r\n\r\n```txt\r\n--- harpoonline ---\r\nPath:   /home/user/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/deps/opt/harpoonline\r\nSource: https://github.com/abeldekat/harpoonline\r\nState:  bd060e8fb3f54b2b75b82eadcb4a6241ea3fc0e2 (v1.2.1)\r\n\r\nMonitor updates from `main`:\r\n<Nothing>\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn preparation for release v1.3.0, there are now 4 commits that have not been retrieved yet.\r\n\r\n`~/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/deps/opt/harpoonline`:\r\n\r\n```txt\r\nharpoonline on  main [⇣] via 🌙 v5.4.6\r\n❯ git log --oneline | head -1\r\nbd060e8 chore(main): release 1.2.1 (#12)\r\n```\r\nAs a consequence, the following line is surprising:\r\n\r\n```txt\r\nMonitor updates from `main`: --> suggests that there are no new commits in main...\r\n<Nothing>\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn this situation, is there an alternative configuration that will show the new commits in main? \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
