            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> `~/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/deps/opt/harpoonline`:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> harpoonline on  main [⇣] via 🌙 v5.4.6\r\n> ❯ git log --oneline | head -1\r\n> bd060e8 chore(main): release 1.2.1 (#12)\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nFirst of all, this looks like a repository that is not completely managed by 'mini.deps', as it does does not check out to branch (and it seems that repo *is* checked out to `main`). So any inconsistency is now assumed to be on the user.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nThe 'mini.deps' uses remote branches directly without local checkout to get necessary info. Monitor log is basically computed like this:\r\n- Get commit of `origin/main` (assuming `main` is a monitor branch).\r\n- Fetch `origin/main`.\r\n- Again get commit of `origin/main`.\r\n- Show the log between current those two commits.\r\n\r\nIt looks like `origin/main` did not change what commit it points to.",
