        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It's indeed Lazygit. The situation occurs when I open Lazygit in `packdir/plugin`. Thanks a lot! \r\n\r\nWhilst testing, I found one scenario where the tag is not checked-out.\r\n\r\nThe repro, `~/.config/repro`:\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>init.lua</summary>\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal function clone(path_to_site)\r\n  local mini_path = path_to_site .. \"pack/deps/start/mini.nvim\"\r\n  if not vim.loop.fs_stat(mini_path) then\r\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\r\n    local clone_cmd =\r\n      { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--filter=blob:none\", \"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim\", mini_path }\r\n    vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\r\n    vim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim | helptags ALL\")\r\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installed `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal path_to_site = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/\"\r\nclone(path_to_site)\r\nlocal MiniDeps = require(\"mini.deps\")\r\nMiniDeps.setup({ path = { package = path_to_site } })\r\nlocal add, now = MiniDeps.add, MiniDeps.now\r\n\r\nvim.g.mapleader = \" \"\r\nnow(function()\r\n  vim.cmd.colorscheme(\"minischeme\")\r\n\r\n  add({ source = \"abeldekat/dummy\", checkout = \"v1.0.0\" })\r\n\r\n  local MiniStatusline = require(\"mini.statusline\")\r\n  MiniStatusline.setup({\r\n    set_vim_settings = false,\r\n  })\r\nend)\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\nSteps:\r\n\r\n1. Create a public project on github: `abeldekat/dummy`\r\n2. Clone the project to ie `~/projects`\r\n3. `cd dummy`\r\n4. `touch one`\r\n5. `git add .`\r\n6. `git commit -m \"one\"`\r\n7. `git push`\r\n8. `git tag -a v1.0.0 -m \"v1.0.0\"`\r\n9. `git push origin --tags`\r\n10. verify on github that both the commit and tag are present\r\n11. `cd ~/.config/repro`\r\n12. `NVIM_APPNAME=repro nvim init.lua`\r\n\r\nIn `~/.local/share/repro/site/pack/deps/opt/dummy`:\r\n\r\n```txt\r\ndummy on  main\r\n❮ git log --oneline | head -1\r\n1a91c7c one\r\n```\r\n`DepsUpdate`:\r\n\r\n```txt\r\n--- dummy ---\r\nPath:   /home/user/.local/share/repro/site/pack/deps/opt/dummy\r\nSource: https://github.com/abeldekat/dummy\r\nState:  1a91c7c1cb7f8d62dc3ff0ed917cfb55bdde760d (v1.0.0)\r\n\r\nMonitor updates from `main`:\r\n<Nothing>\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Summary**: mini.deps did not check out tag v1.0.0. The project has only one commit and one tag.\r\n\r\nMore steps:\r\n\r\n1. Add a new commit \"two\" and push\r\n2. `rm -rf ~/.local/state/repro ~/.local/share/repro ~/.cache/repro`\r\n3. `NVIM_APPNAME=repro nvim init.lua`\r\n4. During installation mini.deps outputs the checkout to v1.0.0\r\n\r\nIn `~/.local/share/repro/site/pack/deps/opt/dummy`\r\n\r\n```txt\r\ndummy (1a91c7c)\r\n❮ git log --oneline\r\n1a91c7c (HEAD, tag: v1.0.0) one\r\n```\r\n\r\n`DepsUpdate`:\r\n\r\n```txt\r\n--- dummy ---\r\nPath:   /home/user/.local/share/repro/site/pack/deps/opt/dummy\r\nSource: https://github.com/abeldekat/dummy\r\nState:  1a91c7c1cb7f8d62dc3ff0ed917cfb55bdde760d (v1.0.0)\r\n\r\nMonitor updates from `main`:\r\n<Nothing>\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Summary**: All is well, when retrieving the plugin from scratch, and it has more than one commit.\r\n",
