            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> In `~/.local/share/repro/site/pack/deps/opt/dummy`:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> dummy on  main\r\n> ❮ git log --oneline | head -1\r\n> 1a91c7c one\r\n> ```\r\n>\r\n> `DepsUpdate`:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> --- dummy ---\r\n> Path:   /home/user/.local/share/repro/site/pack/deps/opt/dummy\r\n> Source: https://github.com/abeldekat/dummy\r\n> State:  1a91c7c1cb7f8d62dc3ff0ed917cfb55bdde760d (v1.0.0)\r\n> \r\n> Monitor updates from `main`:\r\n> <Nothing>\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> **Summary**: mini.deps did not check out tag v1.0.0. The project has only one commit and one tag.\r\n\r\nI am confused. Both shell and 'mini.deps' confirmation buffer show that it is checked to the commit of `v1.0.0`. If you mean that It does not point to the exact hash of `v1.0.0` tag, then I don't think that should make a difference.\r\n\r\nIf you mean that \"Monitor updates from `main`\" is empty after initial clone, then it is to be expected as there is nothing to compare to yet.",
