        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I mean that in the first case, mini.deps does not **actually** checkout to \"v1.0.0\". In the second case, from scratch where two commits are present, it does checkout to \"v1.0.0\".\r\n> \r\n> First case: Inside packdir, the branch is main Second case: Inside packdir: `HEAD detached at 1a91c7c`\r\n> Second case: Inside packdir: `HEAD detached at 1a91c7c`\r\n\r\nAh, I understand what you mean. The logic here is the same as with tags: the goal is to make sure that `HEAD` *eventually* points to the commit it is supposed to point. It does not detach `HEAD` in this case because initially after clone it already points to where it needs to be pointed.\r\n\r\nAlthough it is indeed a not 100% consistent \"always have detached `HEAD`\" behavior, it is consistent where it matters (\"always make `HEAD` point to the proper target commit\").",
